  "slug": "astrometric-precision-incoherent-4af7",
  "summary": "New HSC-Y3 shear, CMB+BAO recombination tests and scalar-tensor reconstructions probe the DESI-era preference for evolving dark energy.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is whether combined late- and early-Universe data prefer dynamical dark energy over ΛCDM. HSC-Y3 cosmic shear combined with DESI BAO, DES SNe and BBN priors yields a 2.4σ preference for a time-varying equation of state. Allowing w0wa removes the hinted early-recombination preference from CMB+BAO and gives the lowest AIC, suggesting the two extensions compete for the same data features. A genetic-algorithm reconstruction of scalar-tensor Lagrangians fit to DESI DR2 BAO, Pantheon+, CMB and fσ8 improves on ΛCDM by Δχ²=-16.6. Systematics and early-Universe inputs are also being revisited: updated CMB acoustic priors separate early-Universe information from lensing and ISW, and DES supernova colour evolution constrains intergalactic dust that could shift distance moduli. Forecasts propose galaxy-CMB and galaxy-galaxy lensing ratios as geometric probes for LSST and Simons Observatory. Separately, axion early dark energy with JWST high-redshift galaxy abundances gives H0≈72.76 km/s/Mpc.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
